# Model profile: Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct
#
# MoE model: 30B total parameters, ~3.3B active per token. Serving still
# requires ALL expert weights resident in VRAM — the 3.3B "active" figure
# describes compute cost per token, not memory footprint. See docs/MODELS.md.
#
# VRAM budget check (why AWQ, not FP8, and why 16K context):
#   - BF16 (2 bytes/param): ~60 GB weights alone — does not fit on a 32 GB card.
#   - FP8 (1 byte/param):   ~30 GB weights alone — leaves ~0 GB for KV cache
#                           inside the 22-24 GB workstation budget, and gfx1201
#                           has no confirmed-working native FP8 kernel path in
#                           the pinned vLLM image as of this writing (silent
#                           FP32 dequant fallback has been reported upstream).
#   - AWQ INT4 (~0.5 byte/param + overhead): ~15.7 GiB weights measured live
#     on scar.lab, leaving headroom for KV cache at 16K context. This is why
#     AWQ is the default here.
#
# MODEL_ID below is a third-party AWQ quantization (not published by Qwen or
# AMD) — accuracy/quality has not been independently verified by this repo.
# Swap it out freely; see docs/MODELS.md for alternatives (official FP8,
# GPTQ-Int8) and why they don't fit the default VRAM budget.
MODEL_ID=stelterlab/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-AWQ
SERVED_MODEL_NAME=qwen3-coder-30b-a3b

# Conservative baseline context (see docs/MODELS.md for 8K/32K test plan).
# The model advertises a much larger native context window; we deliberately
# start well below it.
MAX_MODEL_LEN=16384

# Fraction of total GPU memory vLLM is allowed to use. Tuned live on scar.lab
# by sweeping 0.72/0.68/0.65 and measuring REAL total VRAM used (rocm-smi,
# not the nominal percentage — real usage runs a few GiB over the nominal
# target due to graph-capture buffers/allocator overhead not captured by
# vLLM's own weights+KV-cache accounting):
#   0.72 -> 25.12 GiB used -> 6.74 GiB desktop reserve, 63,152 KV tokens (3.85x @16K)
#   0.68 -> 23.88 GiB used -> 7.98 GiB desktop reserve, 50,400 KV tokens (3.08x @16K)  <- chosen
#   0.65 -> 22.80 GiB used -> 9.06 GiB desktop reserve, 39,792 KV tokens (2.43x @16K)
# 0.68 was chosen: it hits the ~7-8 GiB desktop-reserve target almost exactly
# while keeping most of the concurrency headroom — 0.65 buys only ~1 GiB more
# reserve for a disproportionate ~21% concurrency cut. Single-stream
# throughput/TTFT were statistically identical across all three (~42-43
# tok/s, ~0.03-0.04s TTFT) — this tradeoff is about concurrency/context
# headroom, not single-request speed. See docs/TUNING.md.
GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION=0.68

# Left empty deliberately — do NOT set this to "awq". Verified live on
# scar.lab: this specific checkpoint (stelterlab, built via llm-compressor)
# is packaged in the newer "compressed-tensors" config format, not the
# legacy AWQ format, and forcing --quantization awq fails hard at startup
# ("Quantization method specified in the model config (compressed-tensors)
# does not match the quantization method specified in the `quantization`
# argument (awq)"). Leave this unset so vLLM reads the method the
# checkpoint actually declares. (Contrast with the 14B profile: that
# checkpoint IS legacy-AWQ-packaged, where forcing awq explicitly matters —
# see the note there. The two profiles needing different handling here is
# itself evidence this needs re-checking per-checkpoint, not assumed.)
QUANTIZATION=

# Leave empty (vLLM default: KV cache dtype matches model compute dtype).
# FP8 KV cache is a possible later tuning experiment, not a conservative
# baseline default — see docs/TUNING.md.
KV_CACHE_DTYPE=

# Explicit KV cache size in bytes (vLLM's --kv-cache-memory-bytes), as an
# alternative to letting GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION derive it. Tested live on
# scar.lab alongside a utilization sweep — GPU_MEMORY_UTILIZATION won out as
# the default because it's the only one of the two that adapts automatically
# per model profile (a fixed byte count tuned for this 30B model's ~15.7 GiB
# weights would be wrong for the 14B profile's ~9.4 GiB weights). Left empty;
# see docs/TUNING.md for the comparison and when you might want this instead.
KV_CACHE_MEMORY_BYTES=

# Tool/function calling. Required for agentic coding tools (OpenCode, etc) —
# without this, any request with tool_choice="auto" fails outright with
# "auto tool choice requires --enable-auto-tool-choice and --tool-call-parser
# to be set" (hit live via OpenCode CLI on scar.lab). qwen3_xml chosen over
# vLLM's qwen3_coder parser: qwen3_coder has a reported bug producing
# runaway "!!!!" output on long inputs containing a tool call; qwen3_xml is
# documented as the more stable choice for Qwen3-Coder specifically. See
# docs/OPENCODE.md.
EXTRA_VLLM_ARGS=--enable-auto-tool-choice --tool-call-parser qwen3_xml
